defmodule <%= @web %>.BubbleData do
  @moduledoc """
  The data the pages scaffolded from Bubble show (WTF-420): a page's
  "Type of content" (its thing, from the URL), the data sources of its
  groups, repeating groups and reusable-element instances, and the
  properties each instance sets (or their defaults, WTF-493). The page's
  `Workflows` module (and each reusable element's) lists them in
  `__bubble__(:data)` with one function per source, in the order they read
  each other; this module runs them, keeps what they return in the
  page's `@bubble_data` and reloads it when a record they read changes.

  ## Data access (opt-in)

<%= if @enforced? do %>  The Ash resources have the privacy policies compiled from Bubble
  (`privacy: :enforced`, WTF-423). Every read goes through Ash with the
  current user as the actor (read afresh at each load,
  `<%= @module %>.Privacy.load_actor/1`) and `authorize?: true`: a record
  the user may not view reads as nothing, a field as empty
  (`%Ash.ForbiddenField{}`), and searches run the `:search` action (what
  the user may find in searches). A read the policies refuse outright
  (e.g. logged out, where every rule reads the user) reads nothing, as
  Bubble shows nothing. Pages still load nothing unless the owner opts in,
  the same switch as the workflows':

      config :<%= @app %>, <%= @web %>.BubbleWorkflows, data_access: true

  **Not guarded:** a search's own constraints are code, and field policies
  do not apply to code: a constraint on a field the user may not view
  still matches its value (the record itself must still be findable).
  Aggregates over hidden fields are not guarded either.<% else %>  The Ash resources are generated with `privacy: :omit`: **no resource has
  an authorizer**, so every read would return every record to anyone who
  can open the page. Pages load nothing unless the owner opts in, the
  same switch as the workflows':

      config :<%= @app %>, <%= @web %>.BubbleWorkflows, data_access: true

  Every read goes through Ash with the current user as the actor and
  `authorize?: true`, which restricts nothing until you add policies.

  **A search that ignores empty constraints can return every record.** A
  page search stating `ignore_empty_constraints: true` drops each
  constraint whose value is empty, as Bubble does (any other empty
  constraint value matches nothing). A signed-in user whose referenced
  field is empty (`X = Current User's Workspace`, with no workspace) or
  whose input is blank gets every record of the type the search can
  read (up to its page size or `:max_items`). A logged-out visitor does
  not: a constraint reading the current user matches nothing for them
  (stricter than Bubble, whose temporary user would drop it). With no
  policies nothing stops this. Before enabling data access, find such
  searches and add policies that limit what each user may read, or
  make the referenced field required, or set the search's
  `ignore_empty_constraints` to false in Bubble where a blank value
  should show nothing; requiring sign-in does not help.<% end %>

  ## What a browser can choose

  Nothing but the page's own state. A page reads only the sources its
  module lists, with their filters fixed in the code; the browser supplies
  input values, custom states and the URL (its parameters and path
  segments, read as Bubble reads them as text, numbers, yes/no or dates,
  pinned into filters as values) and the unique IDs of things in the URL
  (the page's thing in its path, a thing parameter), which must look like
  a Bubble ID and are read through Ash like any other record, as the
  current user. No event or URL names a resource, a field, a record's
  type or a query, and nothing from the browser becomes an atom.

  ## Bounds

  A repeating group shows its first page (its rows times its columns); a
  list with no page size, or a larger one, stops at `:max_items`
  (`config :<%= @app %>, <%= @web %>.BubbleData, max_items: 100`). A
  search's `count` is <%= if @enforced? do %>the number of keys read through `:search`, at most
  `:max_count` (`max_count/0`: Ash's count aggregate under-counts with
  policies that read the user)<% else %>a count query<% end %>. A list of things stored as IDs is
  read by ID, at most the page size capped by `:max_items`. A
  relationship the page's bindings read through a record (its related
  list) reads at most `related_cap/0` records (`:max_items`, at most 100)
  per record, in all when lists nest (a record's tasks' comments share it).

  ## Each read once (WTF-501)

  A page load reads the current user once at mount for its first load
  (a later load, a patch or an event reads them again; the page-loaded
  workflows, which may write, read the actor again). One read of the page's data (`read_pass/1`) makes each
  query, each read of things by unique ID and each relationship load
  once, as that user, however many sources ask for it (the current
  user's relationships, a search two elements share, the same records'
  relationships in every cell's instance), and forgets it when it ends:
  the next read (a change notification, an event) reads again. The
  records of a list that holds none are nothing, without a query.

  ## Random order

  A search sorted by Bubble's random sort reads its records ordered by
  the MD5 of each one's primary key and a seed (`random_sort/1`): the
  database orders and limits (the page size, `:max_items`), so a list
  shows a random selection, not the first records shuffled. The seed is
  new on every read, so the order changes whenever the page reads again
  (a change notification included), as Bubble's does on every load. Tests
  fix it (`config :<%= @app %>, <%= @web %>.BubbleData, random_seed:
  "seed"`, set in `config/test.exs`) for a deterministic order. It reads
  no field but the primary key: <%= if @enforced? do %>the policies (and the
  search fields check) apply as to any other search<% else %>nothing to guard<% end %>.

  ## Reactivity

  When loaded (and connected), the page subscribes to one topic per data
  type it searches (a record of that type created, changed or deleted)
  and one per record it holds (`<%= @module %>.Bubble.Changes`, published
  by the resources' `Ash.Notifier.PubSub`), and reloads its data when any
  fires. Only a topic name travels, never a record: the page reads again
  with its own actor.

  The page reads again only when its data is stale (`@bubble_data_stale`):
  a change notification of a topic it subscribes to, a data step of its
  workflows (`<%= @web %>.BubbleWorkflows.backend/2`), or a custom state or
  input its workflows changed (they may be search constraints). An event
  whose workflows change none of that reads nothing, and a "do every"
  tick or a scheduled custom event that changes nothing reads nothing.
  Every read clears the flag and takes the change notifications already
  delivered to the page (sent after their writes committed, so the read
  sees them): a workflow's own write and its notification are one read.

  An input change (typing, WTF-475) is narrower: it reads again only the
  sources whose value or search constraints read that input (a source's
  `inputs` in `__bubble__(:data)`) and the sources reading those
  (`reads`, `cell`), transitively; the rest of the page's data stays as
  it is, as read by the same current user: when the user differs from
  the one the page was read as (a changed role, or anything the policies
  read), the whole page reads again. The browser debounces typing
  (`phx-debounce`, 300 ms) and the page coalesces what still arrives into
  one read (`defer/2`). A source listed without `inputs` (scaffolded
  before WTF-475) is read again on any input change, with the rest of the
  page.

  ## Display data (WTF-492)

  An element a "Display data" or "Display list" step set
  (`<%= @web %>.BubbleWorkflows.display/8`, kept in `@bubble_displayed`
  until a reset or the page's next load) shows what the step showed, in
  place of its own source (`display:` in its `__bubble__(:data)` entry;
  `read: :displayed` when it has no source of its own). The page kept a
  thing's unique ID only: it is read again through Ash as the current
  user, like any other read, so a workflow never shows what the user may
  not read<%= if @enforced? do %> (a record the policies hide shows nothing, a hidden field is
  empty)<% end %>; anything kept that is not a text shaped like a Bubble ID
  shows nothing (`show/3`). In a repeating group's cell it is kept by the
  cell's thing, not its position. A list shows at most its page size, capped by
  `:max_items`.

  ## Reusable instances in repeating group cells (WTF-494)

  An instance in a cell (`__bubble__(:cells)`) has a scope per cell, the
  cell's thing's (`<%= @web %>.Bubble.cell_scope/4`): its thing and the
  properties it sets are computed in the cell, and its reusable element's
  sources run in that scope. Each source is read for every cell together,
  never once per cell: what its value reads through relationships is
  loaded for all the cells first (`preloads`), things given as unique IDs
  are read at once, the relationships the bindings read load once per
  resource, and a source that reads nothing of its scope (`shared`) runs
  once. The cells are the list as the current user read it: a thing the
  user may not read has no cell, no instance and no scope, and the page
  accepts events only in the scopes it read (`@bubble_cells`). At most
  three levels of instances in cells (`max_cell_depth/0`) and `max_cells/0`
  scopes (the first ones; logged once past that).

  ## Searches in cells (WTF-520)

  A search a repeating group's cells read with the cell's thing ("Search
  for orders where customer = Current cell's customer", its `count`, its
  first item, a list of the records a cell's list holds) is read for every
  cell together, never once per cell (`cell_read/4`): the loader runs the
  source in every cell first, collecting each cell's search, then reads
  one query per round of cells with each key compared with every cell's
  values (`customer_id in ^values`; with two or three keys, the cells' own
  combinations of them) and gives each cell the records whose keys are
  its own, in the search's order. Cells whose other constraints differ
  (whether a value is empty) are read in one query each way. A first item
  is the first record per key (`DISTINCT ON`). Otherwise each cell's page
  size is its own: the query reads at most the sum of the cells' page
  sizes (plus one), and the cells a heavier one left short are read again
  together, the limit doubled each round. A `count` reads the keys of at
  most `:max_batched` records (default 10,000), past which each cell's
  count is read on its own. Past `:max_cell_rounds` rounds (default 4),
  what is left is read cell by cell; both are logged. A batched read that
  fails leaves every cell of it empty (logged), as each cell's own would.
  The query reads as the current user, like the cell's own search
  would<%= if @enforced? do %>, through the same action and policies (the search fields check
  sees the same constraints)<% end %>.

  ## Repeating groups in a repeating group's cell (WTF-520)

  A repeating group in another's cell (two levels) is read per outer
  cell: its list is a value per outer cell (`{scope, inner, outer
  index}`), its search read for every outer cell together. Its cells'
  sources (`outer` in `__bubble__(:data)`) run for every inner cell of
  every outer cell together, never once per outer cell: their values are
  kept in the outer cell's scope (`<%= @web %>.Bubble.cell_scope/4`),
  what they read through the inner and outer cells' things is loaded for
  all of them first (`cell_loads`, `outer_loads`, `preloads`), and their
  searches are batched across all of them. The reusable instances in
  inner cells (`{{outer, inner}, ...}` in `__bubble__(:cells)`) get a
  scope per inner cell, by the inner cell's thing in the outer cell's
  scope; the page accepts events only in the scopes it read.

  ## Unverified Bubble behavior

  To confirm by replay (WTF-358): a page's thing is read from the URL path
  segment after the page name (`/<page>/<unique id>`; Bubble also accepts
  a slug, which is not read here); a search that does not state whether
  it ignores empty constraints is not generated (see
  `docs/page-data.md`); a repeating group's later pages are not loaded;
  "Display data" wins over an element's own source until a reset or the
  page's next load, even when what the source reads changes.
  """

  require Ash.Expr
  require Ash.Query
  require Logger

  import Phoenix.Component, only: [assign: 3]
  import Phoenix.LiveView, only: [connected?: 1]

  alias <%= @module %>.Bubble.Changes
  alias <%= @module %>.Workflows.Runtime
  alias <%= @web %>.Bubble
  alias <%= @web %>.BubbleWorkflows

  @id ~r/\A[0-9]{1,20}x[0-9]{1,24}\z/
  @pass {__MODULE__, :read_pass}
  @collect {__MODULE__, :cell_reads}
  @unread {__MODULE__, :cell_unread}

  @doc "Whether pages may read stored data (the workflows' opt-in)."
  def data_access?,
    do:
      Keyword.get(Application.get_env(:<%= @app %>, BubbleWorkflows, []), :data_access) == true

  @doc "The most items a list reads (`:max_items`, default 100)."
  def max_items do
    case Keyword.get(Application.get_env(:<%= @app %>, __MODULE__, []), :max_items, 100) do
      n when is_integer(n) and n > 0 -> n
      _ -> 100
    end
  end

  @doc """
  Bubble's random sort (see "Random order"): `query` (or a resource)
  ordered by the MD5
  of the primary key and `random_seed/0`, before its limit. With a
  composite primary key only its first column is hashed: records sharing
  it keep the database's order among themselves.
  """
  def random_sort(query) do
    # A filter of `true` leaves the resource module as it is.
    query = Ash.Query.new(query)
    [pk | _] = Ash.Resource.Info.primary_key(query.resource)
    key = Ash.Expr.ref(pk)
    seed = random_seed()

    order = Ash.Expr.calc(fragment("md5(CAST(? AS text) || ?)", ^key, ^seed), type: :string)
    Ash.Query.sort(query, [{order, :asc}])
  end

  @doc """
  The seed of `random_sort/1`: `:random_seed` when configured (text, for
  tests), a new one for every read otherwise.
  """
  def random_seed do
    case Keyword.get(Application.get_env(:<%= @app %>, __MODULE__, []), :random_seed) do
      seed when is_binary(seed) and seed != "" -> seed
      _ -> Base.encode16(:crypto.strong_rand_bytes(8))
    end
  end

<%= if @enforced? do %>  @doc """
  The most records a page `count` reads (`:max_count`, default 10_000): a
  count reads the keys of what it counts, and shows this cap past it.
  """
  def max_count do
    case Keyword.get(Application.get_env(:<%= @app %>, __MODULE__, []), :max_count, 10_000) do
      n when is_integer(n) and n > 0 -> n
      _ -> 10_000
    end
  end

<% end %>  @doc """
  The unique ID of a page's thing from the URL path parameter
  (`bubble_thing`): a Bubble ID, else nil.
  """
  def thing_id(%{"bubble_thing" => id}, path)
      when is_binary(id) and byte_size(id) <= 64 and is_binary(path) do
    if List.last(String.split(path, "/", trim: true)) == id and Regex.match?(@id, id), do: id
  end

  def thing_id(_params, _path), do: nil

  # --- loading --------------------------------------------------------------------------

  @doc """
  Loads the page's data into `@bubble_data` (nothing with data access
  off) and, once connected, subscribes to the changes of what it read.
  The data is then current (`@bubble_data_stale` false). <%= if @enforced? do %>The current
  user is read afresh first, unless `actor_fresh?: true` says the caller
  has just done it (`BubbleWorkflows.refresh_actor/1`).<% else %>`opts` is
  for the enforced variant (`actor_fresh?:`), ignored here.<% end %>
  """
  def load(socket, page, opts \\ []) do
    socket =
      socket
      |> assign(:bubble_data_stale, false)
      |> assign(:bubble_data_inputs, MapSet.new())<%= if @enforced? do %>

    socket =
      if data_access?() and not Keyword.get(opts, :actor_fresh?, false),
        do: BubbleWorkflows.refresh_actor(socket),
        else: socket<% else %>

    _ = opts<% end %>

    if data_access?() and connected?(socket) do
      # Notifications already delivered were sent after their writes
      # committed: this read covers them.
      _ = take_changes(Map.get(socket.assigns, :bubble_topics, MapSet.new()), false)

      {data, by_source, cells} =
        read_pass(fn ->
          {data, by_source} =
            load_surfaces(socket, BubbleWorkflows.surfaces(page), {%{}, %{}}, nil)

          # The reusable instances in cells (WTF-494): one scope per cell read.
          load_cells(socket, page, {data, by_source})
        end)

      socket
      |> assign(:bubble_data, data)
      |> BubbleWorkflows.put_cells(cells)
      |> assign(:bubble_data_actor, data_actor(socket))
      |> assign(:bubble_source_topics, by_source)
      |> subscribe(all_topics(by_source))
    else
      if not data_access?() and connected?(socket) and
           not Map.get(socket.assigns, :bubble_data_warned, false) and sources?(page) do
        Logger.warning(
          "bubble page data not loaded: data access is off " <>
            "(config :<%= @app %>, #{inspect(BubbleWorkflows)}, data_access: true)"
        )
      end

      socket
      |> assign(:bubble_data, %{})
      |> BubbleWorkflows.put_cells([])
      |> assign(:bubble_data_warned, not data_access?() and connected?(socket))
    end
  end

  @doc """
  A change notification: for a subscribed topic, marks the data stale and
  coalesces a burst into one read.
  """
  def changed(socket, topic) do
    topics = Map.get(socket.assigns, :bubble_topics, MapSet.new())

    cond do
      not data_access?() or not MapSet.member?(topics, topic) -> socket
      is_nil(socket.assigns[:bubble_data_refresh]) -> socket |> mark_stale() |> defer(25)
      true -> mark_stale(socket)
    end
  end

  @doc "Marks the page's data stale: the next `reload/2` reads it again."
  def mark_stale(socket), do: assign(socket, :bubble_data_stale, true)

  @doc """
  Marks the inputs `elements` (Bubble IDs) changed: the next `reload/2`
  reads again only the sources that read them, transitively (WTF-475).
  """
  def mark_inputs(socket, elements) do
    changed = Map.get(socket.assigns, :bubble_data_inputs) || MapSet.new()
    assign(socket, :bubble_data_inputs, Enum.into(elements, changed))
  end

  @doc """
  Reads the page's data again only when it is stale, or when a change
  notification of a subscribed topic is already waiting (e.g. the echo of
  a write the event just made outside the workflow runtime). After input
  changes alone (`mark_inputs/2`) it reads only the sources that read
  them.
  """
  def reload(socket, page, opts \\ []) do
    topics = Map.get(socket.assigns, :bubble_topics, MapSet.new())
    waiting? = take_changes(topics, false)
    inputs = Map.get(socket.assigns, :bubble_data_inputs) || MapSet.new()

    cond do
      waiting? or Map.get(socket.assigns, :bubble_data_stale, false) -> load(socket, page, opts)
      MapSet.size(inputs) > 0 -> load_inputs(socket, page, inputs)
      true -> socket
    end
  end

  # Reads again the sources that read the changed inputs, and those that
  # read them; keeps the rest, which were read as the same actor. The
  # current user is the one the event read on its way in (never read again
  # here): when it differs from the one the data was read as (a changed
  # role, or anything else the policies read), the whole page reads again.
  # The subscriptions follow what each source last read.
  defp load_inputs(socket, page, changed) do
    socket = assign(socket, :bubble_data_inputs, MapSet.new())
    affected = affected(socket, page, changed)

    cond do
      not (data_access?() and connected?(socket)) or affected == :all ->
        load(socket, page, actor_fresh?: true)

      data_actor(socket) != Map.get(socket.assigns, :bubble_data_actor) ->
        load(socket, page, actor_fresh?: true)

      MapSet.size(affected) == 0 ->
        socket

      # A list whose cells hold reusable instances (WTF-494): its cells,
      # and so the instances' scopes, may change.
      Enum.any?(cell_lists(socket, page), &MapSet.member?(affected, &1)) ->
        load(socket, page, actor_fresh?: true)

      true ->
        data =
          Map.reject(socket.assigns.bubble_data, fn {key, _} ->
            MapSet.member?(affected, elem(key, 1))
          end)

        by_source = Map.get(socket.assigns, :bubble_source_topics, %{})

        {data, by_source, cells} =
          read_pass(fn ->
            {data, by_source} =
              load_surfaces(socket, BubbleWorkflows.surfaces(page), {data, by_source}, affected)

            load_cells(socket, page, {data, by_source}, affected)
          end)

        socket
        |> assign(:bubble_data, data)
        |> BubbleWorkflows.put_cells(cells)
        |> assign(:bubble_source_topics, by_source)
        |> subscribe(all_topics(by_source))
    end
  end

  @doc """
  Runs `fun` as one read (WTF-501): a read of the page's data (a load, or
  an input's sources read again) or a check of the page's conditions,
  during which nothing is written. In it, the same read as the same actor
  (`once/3`: a query, things by unique ID, the current user's
  relationships) is made once, however many sources or conditions make
  it, and it is forgotten when `fun` returns: the next read (another
  event, a change notification) reads again.
  """
  def read_pass(fun) do
    previous = Process.put(@pass, %{})

    try do
      fun.()
    after
      if previous, do: Process.put(@pass, previous), else: Process.delete(@pass)
    end
  end

  # The actor the page's data is read as.
  defp data_actor(socket),
    do: <%= if @enforced? do %>BubbleWorkflows.current_actor(socket)<% else %>socket.assigns[:current_user]<% end %>

  defp all_topics(by_source),
    do: by_source |> Map.values() |> Enum.reduce(MapSet.new(), &MapSet.union/2)

  # The elements of the sources an input change makes read again: those
  # reading a changed input, then those reading them (their data, or the
  # list of the repeating group whose cells they fill), to a fixpoint.
  # `:all` when a source does not say what it reads.
  defp affected(socket, page, changed) do
    sources =
      for {_scope, m} <- socket |> BubbleWorkflows.surfaces(page) |> Enum.uniq_by(&elem(&1, 1)),
          s <- sources(m),
          do: s

    if Enum.all?(sources, &is_list(Map.get(&1, :inputs))) do
      direct =
        for s <- sources,
            Enum.any?(s.inputs, &MapSet.member?(changed, &1)),
            into: MapSet.new(),
            do: s.element

      spread(sources, direct)
    else
      :all
    end
  end

  defp spread(sources, affected) do
    marked = Enum.reduce(sources, affected, &mark_instance(&1, &2))

    next =
      for s <- sources,
          not MapSet.member?(affected, s.element),
          Enum.any?([s.cell | Map.get(s, :reads, [])], &MapSet.member?(marked, &1)),
          into: affected,
          do: s.element

    if MapSet.size(next) == MapSet.size(affected), do: affected, else: spread(sources, next)
  end

  # The repeating groups whose cells hold reusable instances (WTF-494),
  # with the outer one of a nested repeating group (WTF-520).
  defp cell_lists(socket, page) do
    for {_scope, m} <- socket |> BubbleWorkflows.surfaces(page) |> Enum.uniq_by(&elem(&1, 1)),
        {rg, _entries} <- BubbleWorkflows.cells(m),
        list <- if(is_tuple(rg), do: Tuple.to_list(rg), else: [rg]),
        uniq: true,
        do: list
  end

  # What reads an instance's thing names the instance as well as its holder.
  defp mark_instance(%{instance: instance, element: e}, set) when is_binary(instance),
    do: if(MapSet.member?(set, e), do: MapSet.put(set, instance), else: set)

  defp mark_instance(_source, set), do: set

  # Takes the change notifications waiting in the page's mailbox; whether
  # one was of a subscribed topic.
  defp take_changes(topics, subscribed?) do
    receive do
      {:bubble, :data_changed, topic} ->
        take_changes(topics, subscribed? or MapSet.member?(topics, topic))
    after
      0 -> subscribed?
    end
  end

  @doc "Debounces input-driven reads; only the latest input values are loaded."
  def defer(socket, delay \\ 150) do
    # A new input supersedes the old timer. Stale queued messages are
    # ignored by pending?/2; notifications leave the pending timer alone.
    ref = make_ref()
    Process.send_after(self(), {:bubble, :data_refresh, ref}, delay)
    assign(socket, :bubble_data_refresh, ref)
  end

  @doc "Whether this is the current (not superseded) refresh timer."
  def pending?(socket, ref), do: not is_nil(ref) and socket.assigns[:bubble_data_refresh] == ref

  @doc """
  Handles the pending refresh: reads when the data is stale (not when a
  read since has covered it); superseded timers do not read. `opts` as
  `load/3`'s.
  """
  def refresh(socket, page, ref, opts \\ []) do
    if pending?(socket, ref) do
      socket
      |> assign(:bubble_data_refresh, nil)
      |> reload(page, opts)
    else
      socket
    end
  end

  defp sources?(page),
    do: Enum.any?(BubbleWorkflows.surfaces(page), fn {_scope, m} -> sources(m) != [] end)

  @doc "The data sources a surface module lists (none for a module scaffolded before WTF-420)."
  def sources(module) do
    module.__bubble__(:data)
  rescue
    FunctionClauseError -> []
  end

  # The page's surfaces (`{scope, module}`: the page, then the instances it
  # renders once), every source or only those whose element is in `only`;
  # the data, and the topics each source's value needs (by source).
  defp load_surfaces(socket, surfaces, acc, only) do
    groups = for {scope, module} <- surfaces, do: %{module: module, scopes: [scope], id: scope}
    run_plan(socket, outer_plan(groups), acc, only)
  end

  # The page's own plan does not depend on its data (the instances it
  # renders once are fixed): computed once per set of modules and kept
  # (`:persistent_term`). A recompiled module (its MD5) is planned again.
  defp outer_plan(groups) do
    key =
      {__MODULE__, :plan,
       :erlang.phash2(for g <- groups, do: {g.scopes, g.module, g.module.module_info(:md5)})}

    case :persistent_term.get(key, nil) do
      nil ->
        steps = plan(groups)
        :persistent_term.put(key, steps)
        steps

      steps ->
        steps
    end
  end

  # Runs the sources of `groups` (a module with the scopes it runs in: one,
  # or the same reusable instance in every cell of a repeating group,
  # WTF-494) in the order they read each other (`plan/1`), each source for
  # every scope of its group together before the next (`load_source/7`). A
  # group's `id` names it in the topics by source.
  defp load_groups(socket, groups, acc, only), do: run_plan(socket, plan(groups), acc, only)

  defp run_plan(socket, steps, acc, only) do
    steps
    |> Enum.reduce(acc, fn {group, source, scopes}, acc ->
      if is_nil(only) or MapSet.member?(only, source.element),
        do: load_source(socket, group, source, scopes, acc),
        else: acc
    end)
  end

  # The order sources are read in, across surfaces (WTF-520): a source
  # after those keeping what it reads (`deps`, in `__bubble__(:data)`): a
  # page's source reading an instance's property after the instance's
  # default, computed inside it; a default after the value the instance
  # may set. Otherwise the listed order: the page's, then each instance's
  # (a surface's own sources before those in its repeating groups' cells).
  # Sources reading each other in a cycle (the generator leaves none) keep
  # the listed order. `{group, source, scopes}`: a scope is dropped where
  # the source reads what nothing on the page keeps for it (an instance's
  # property from outside, in a scope the page does not render) or what is
  # dropped itself, so it never reads an empty value in place of one it
  # was not given. A module listing no `deps` (scaffolded before) keeps
  # the listed order. Public for the generated tests only.
  @doc false
  def plan(groups) do
    nodes =
      for group <- groups,
          source <- group.module |> sources() |> own_first(),
          do: %{group: group, source: source}

    nodes = nodes |> Enum.with_index() |> Enum.map(fn {node, i} -> Map.put(node, :i, i) end)

    if Enum.all?(nodes, &is_list(Map.get(&1.source, :deps))),
      do: nodes |> order_nodes() |> with_scopes(),
      else: Enum.map(nodes, &{&1.group, &1.source, &1.group.scopes})
  end

  # A surface's own sources before those in its cells (they read the lists).
  defp own_first(sources) do
    {cells, own} = Enum.split_with(sources, & &1.cell)
    own ++ cells
  end

  # What a source keeps in `scope`: its value (an instance's under the
  # instance's scope), or, in a repeating group's cell, a value per cell.
  defp written(%{cell: cell, element: e}, scope) when is_binary(cell), do: {scope, e, :cells}
  defp written(%{instance: i, element: e}, scope) when is_binary(i), do: {Bubble.nest(scope, i), e}
  defp written(%{element: e}, scope), do: {scope, e}

  defp wanted({:data, path, e}, scope), do: {nest_path(scope, path), e}
  defp wanted({:cell, rg}, scope), do: {scope, rg}
  defp wanted({:cell_data, g}, scope), do: {scope, g, :cells}

  # An instance's property read from outside it: some source must keep it.
  defp needed?({:data, [_ | _], "param_" <> _}), do: true
  defp needed?(_dep), do: false

  defp order_nodes(nodes) do
    writers =
      Enum.reduce(nodes, %{}, fn node, acc ->
        Enum.reduce(node.group.scopes, acc, fn scope, acc ->
          Map.update(acc, written(node.source, scope), [node.i], &[node.i | &1])
        end)
      end)

    # Each node's predecessors: who keeps what it reads; for a default
    # (`default: true`), also the value an instance sets under its key.
    preds =
      Map.new(nodes, fn node ->
        read =
          for scope <- node.group.scopes,
              dep <- node.source.deps,
              w <- Map.get(writers, wanted(dep, scope), []),
              do: w

        own =
          if Map.get(node.source, :default, false),
            do:
              for(
                scope <- node.group.scopes,
                w <- Map.get(writers, written(node.source, scope), []),
                do: w
              ),
            else: []

        {node.i, (read ++ own) |> Enum.reject(&(&1 == node.i)) |> Enum.uniq()}
      end)

    by_i = Map.new(nodes, &{&1.i, &1})

    succs =
      Enum.reduce(preds, %{}, fn {i, ps}, acc ->
        Enum.reduce(ps, acc, fn p, acc -> Map.update(acc, p, [i], &[i | &1]) end)
      end)

    degree = Map.new(preds, fn {i, ps} -> {i, length(ps)} end)
    ready = :gb_sets.from_list(for {i, 0} <- degree, do: i)
    {order, left} = kahn_nodes(ready, degree, succs, [])

    # A cycle (the generator marks them): what is left, in listed order.
    rest = left |> Map.keys() |> Enum.sort()
    {Enum.map(Enum.reverse(order) ++ rest, &by_i[&1]), writers}
  end

  defp kahn_nodes(ready, degree, succs, order) do
    if :gb_sets.is_empty(ready) do
      {order, degree}
    else
      {i, ready} = :gb_sets.take_smallest(ready)
      degree = Map.delete(degree, i)

      {ready, degree} =
        succs
        |> Map.get(i, [])
        |> Enum.reduce({ready, degree}, fn s, {ready, degree} ->
          case Map.fetch(degree, s) do
            {:ok, 1} -> {:gb_sets.add(s, ready), Map.put(degree, s, 0)}
            {:ok, d} -> {ready, Map.put(degree, s, d - 1)}
            :error -> {ready, degree}
          end
        end)

      kahn_nodes(ready, degree, succs, [i | order])
    end
  end

  # The scopes each source runs in, in order: not where what it reads is
  # kept by nothing (`needed?/1`) or by sources dropped there.
  defp with_scopes({ordered, writers}) do
    {steps, _kept} =
      Enum.map_reduce(ordered, MapSet.new(), fn node, kept ->
        scopes =
          Enum.filter(node.group.scopes, fn scope ->
            Enum.all?(node.source.deps, fn dep ->
              key = wanted(dep, scope)

              case Map.get(writers, key, []) -- [node.i] do
                [] -> Map.has_key?(writers, key) or not needed?(dep)
                _others -> MapSet.member?(kept, key)
              end
            end)
          end)

        kept = Enum.reduce(scopes, kept, &MapSet.put(&2, written(node.source, &1)))
        {{node.group, node.source, scopes}, kept}
      end)

    steps
  end

  # One source of a group, in `scopes` (those of the group it runs in).
  # Read together (more than one scope, WTF-494), a source never queries
  # once per scope: see `read_source/7`.
  defp load_source(_socket, _group, _source, [], acc), do: acc

  defp load_source(socket, group, %{cell: nil} = source, scopes, acc) do
    units =
      for scope <- scopes do
        key_scope = if source.instance, do: Bubble.nest(scope, source.instance), else: scope
        key = {key_scope, source.element}
        %{scope: scope, cell: nil, key: key, shown: key}
      end

    read_source(socket, group.module, source, units, acc, group.id, length(group.scopes) > 1)
  end

  # A group in a repeating group's cell holds a value per cell, and so
  # does an instance there (its thing and properties, under its scope in
  # that cell, WTF-494): read for every cell together.
  defp load_source(socket, group, source, scopes, {data, _by_source} = acc) do
    units =
      case Map.get(source, :outer) do
        nil ->
          for scope <- scopes, {item, i} <- cell_items(data, scope, source.cell) do
            cell_unit(scope, source, item, i)
          end

        # In a repeating group rendered per cell of another (WTF-520):
        # every inner cell of every outer cell, read together.
        outer ->
          for scope <- scopes,
              {outer_item, oi} <- cell_items(data, scope, outer),
              outer_scope = Bubble.cell_scope(scope, outer, outer_item, oi),
              {item, i} <- nested_items(data, scope, source.cell, oi) do
            outer_scope
            |> cell_unit(source, item, i)
            |> Map.merge(%{scope: scope, nested: {{outer_item, oi}, outer_scope}})
          end
      end

    # The relationships the source reads through the cell's thing (and,
    # in a nested repeating group's cell, the outer cell's), for every
    # cell at once, read as the current user.
    items =
      units
      |> Enum.map(fn %{cell: {item, _}} -> item end)
      |> load_values(source.cell_loads, data_actor(socket))

    units =
      units
      |> Enum.zip_with(items, fn %{cell: {_, i}} = unit, item -> %{unit | cell: {item, i}} end)
      |> load_outer(Map.get(source, :outer_loads, []), data_actor(socket))

    read_source(socket, group.module, source, units, acc, group.id, true)
  end

  # The items of a repeating group's list, with their 1-based index.
  defp cell_items(data, scope, rg) do
    case Map.get(data, {scope, rg}) do
      list when is_list(list) -> Enum.with_index(list, 1)
      _ -> []
    end
  end

  # The outer cells' things of nested units (WTF-520) with `loads`, each
  # outer cell's loaded once for all its inner cells.
  defp load_outer(units, [], _actor), do: units

  defp load_outer(units, loads, actor) do
    outer = units |> Enum.map(fn %{nested: {{item, _}, _}} -> item end) |> Enum.uniq()
    loaded = Map.new(Enum.zip(outer, load_values(outer, loads, actor)))

    Enum.map(units, fn %{nested: {{item, oi}, cell_scope}} = unit ->
      %{unit | nested: {{Map.fetch!(loaded, item), oi}, cell_scope}}
    end)
  end

  # The items of a repeating group rendered per cell of another (WTF-520),
  # in the outer cell `index`: its list there, a value per outer cell.
  defp nested_items(data, scope, rg, index) do
    case Map.get(data, {scope, rg, index}) do
      list when is_list(list) -> Enum.with_index(list, 1)
      _ -> []
    end
  end

  # A cell's value: a group's by the cell's index (what "Display data"
  # showed in it by the cell's thing, WTF-492, so a re-sorted list keeps
  # what each thing's cell showed); an instance's (WTF-494) under its scope
  # in the cell, the cell's thing's.
  # In a nested repeating group's cell (WTF-520), `scope` is the outer
  # cell's: the inner cells' values are kept there.
  defp cell_unit(scope, %{instance: instance} = source, item, i) when is_binary(instance) do
    key = {Bubble.nest(Bubble.cell_scope(scope, source.cell, item, i), instance), source.element}
    %{scope: scope, cell: {item, i}, nested: nil, key: key, shown: key}
  end

  defp cell_unit(scope, source, item, i),
    do: %{
      scope: scope,
      cell: {item, i},
      nested: nil,
      key: {scope, source.element, i},
      shown: {scope, source.element, {:cell, Runtime.id(item)}}
    }

  # One source in every unit (`%{scope, cell, key, shown}`): its value is
  # kept under `key`. A reusable element property's default is only for
  # the instances that set no value (theirs is read first, where they
  # are). Read together (`batch?`, WTF-494), a source never queries once
  # per unit: what its value reads through relationships is loaded first
  # for every unit (`preloads`), a thing it gives as a unique ID is read
  # with the others' (`records/5`), its own relationships load for every
  # unit at once, and one that reads nothing of its scope (`shared`) runs
  # once.
  defp read_source(socket, module, source, units, {data, by_source}, id, batch?) do
    units =
      if Map.get(source, :default, false),
        do: Enum.reject(units, &Map.has_key?(data, &1.key)),
        else: units

    {data, states, batch} = preload(socket, source, units, data, batch?)
    actor = data_actor(socket)
    displayed = Map.get(socket.assigns, :bubble_displayed) || %{}
    shared = if batch? and Map.get(source, :shared, false), do: :pending

    # Its searches read with each cell's values (WTF-520): collected in
    # every unit first, then read once per round for all of them.
    if batch? and Map.get(source, :cell_reads, false) and source.read != :displayed do
      collect_cells(
        fn ->
          for unit <- units, not Map.has_key?(displayed, unit.shown) do
            # What a unit reads after a search not read yet may depend on it.
            Process.delete(@unread)
            run(module, source, unit_ctx(socket, module, unit, data, states, batch))
          end
        end,
        actor
      )
    end

    {values, _shared} =
      Enum.map_reduce(units, shared, fn unit, shared ->
        ctx = unit_ctx(socket, module, unit, data, states, batch)

        case Map.fetch(displayed, unit.shown) do
          {:ok, shown} ->
            {{unit, {:ok, shown(shown, source, ctx)}}, shared}

          :error when source.read == :displayed ->
            {{unit, :none}, shared}

          :error ->
            case shared do
              {:done, value} ->
                {{unit, {:ok, value}}, shared}

              :pending ->
                value = run(module, source, ctx)
                {{unit, {:ok, value}}, {:done, value}}

              nil ->
                {{unit, {:ok, run(module, source, ctx)}}, nil}
            end
        end
      end)

    values = if batch?, do: settle(values, source, actor), else: values

    {data, topics} =
      Enum.reduce(values, {data, MapSet.new()}, fn
        {unit, {:ok, value}}, {data, topics} ->
          {Map.put(data, unit.key, value), topics(topics, source, value)}

        {_unit, :none}, acc ->
          acc
      end)

    {data, Map.put(by_source, {id, source.instance, source.element, source.fun}, topics)}
  end

  # In a batch, the context carries what `preload/5` read (`batch`); the
  # actor stays the one the policies authorize.
  defp unit_ctx(socket, module, unit, data, states, batch) do
    ctx =
      BubbleWorkflows.data_ctx(socket, module, unit.scope, data, unit.cell, Map.get(unit, :nested))

    if batch, do: %{ctx | batch: batch, states: states}, else: ctx
  end

  # Before a source runs in every unit (WTF-494): what its value reads
  # through relationships (the current user's, a custom state's, a source's
  # it reads), read again for every unit at once, through Ash with the
  # current user as the actor (never reused from what was loaded before:
  # the current user's own relationships are loaded for the policies,
  # without authorization; the current user's are read as the user once
  # per read of the page's data, `actor_loads/2`). Each unit's
  # `load_value/3` then finds them:
  # the records read, each with the paths read through it
  # (`batch.loaded`), and the current user's in a copy (`batch.actor`,
  # with `batch.actor_paths`), never in the actor the policies read.
  defp preload(socket, source, units, data, batch?) do
    actor = data_actor(socket)
    states = Map.get(socket.assigns, :bubble_states) || %{}

    if batch? do
      init = {data, states, %{actor: nil, actor_paths: MapSet.new(), loaded: %{}}}

      Enum.reduce(Map.get(source, :preloads, []), init, fn
        {:actor, loads}, {data, states, batch} ->
          # Read as the current user for this batch, never the actor the
          # policies read; once per read of the page's data for the same
          # paths (`actor_loads/2`, WTF-501).
          copy = actor_loads(actor, loads)
          {data, states, %{batch | actor: copy, actor_paths: Enum.into(loads, batch.actor_paths)}}

        {:data, path, element, loads}, {data, states, batch} ->
          keys = Enum.uniq(for u <- units, do: {nest_path(u.scope, path), element})
          {data, batch} = load_keys(data, keys, loads, actor, batch)
          {data, states, batch}

        {:state, path, element, state, loads}, {data, states, batch} ->
          keys = Enum.uniq(for u <- units, do: {nest_path(u.scope, path), element, state})
          {states, batch} = load_keys(states, keys, loads, actor, batch)
          {data, states, batch}

        {:cell_data, group, loads}, {data, states, batch} ->
          keys = Enum.uniq(for %{cell: {_, i}} = u <- units, do: {cells_scope(u), group, i})
          {data, batch} = load_keys(data, keys, loads, actor, batch)
          {data, states, batch}

        # In a nested repeating group's cell (WTF-520): what a group of the
        # outer cell holds there.
        {:outer_cell_data, group, loads}, {data, states, batch} ->
          keys = Enum.uniq(for %{nested: {{_, oi}, _}} = u <- units, do: {u.scope, group, oi})
          {data, batch} = load_keys(data, keys, loads, actor, batch)
          {data, states, batch}
      end)
    else
      {data, states, nil}
    end
  end

  defp nest_path(scope, path), do: Enum.reduce(path, scope, &Bubble.nest(&2, &1))

  # Where a unit's cells keep their values: the outer cell's scope in a
  # nested repeating group's cell (WTF-520), else the unit's.
  defp cells_scope(%{nested: {_outer, cell_scope}}), do: cell_scope
  defp cells_scope(unit), do: unit.scope

  # The values under `keys` read again with `loads`; each record read is
  # kept in the batch with the paths read through it.
  defp load_keys(map, keys, loads, actor, batch) do
    present = Enum.filter(keys, &Map.has_key?(map, &1))
    loaded = load_values(Enum.map(present, &Map.fetch!(map, &1)), loads, actor)
    {Map.merge(map, Map.new(Enum.zip(present, loaded))), keep_loaded(batch, loaded, loads)}
  end

  # Each record of `loaded` kept in the batch with the paths read through it.
  defp keep_loaded(batch, loaded, loads) do
    read =
      loaded
      |> Enum.flat_map(&records_in/1)
      |> Enum.reduce(batch.loaded, fn record, acc ->
        case record_key(record) do
          nil ->
            acc

          key ->
            paths = acc |> Map.get(key, {record, MapSet.new()}) |> elem(1)
            Map.put(acc, key, {record, Enum.into(loads, paths)})
        end
      end)

    %{batch | loaded: read}
  end

  defp record_key(%{__struct__: module, id: id}) when not is_nil(id), do: {module, id}
  defp record_key(_record), do: nil

  # Read together: the things given as unique IDs read at once (one read
  # per resource), then the relationships the page's bindings read through
  # the source, for every unit at once.
  defp settle(values, source, actor) do
    values
    |> resolve(actor)
    |> then(fn values ->
      loaded =
        values
        |> Enum.map(fn
          {_unit, {:ok, value}} -> value
          {_unit, :none} -> nil
        end)
        |> load_values(source.loads, actor)

      Enum.zip_with(values, loaded, fn
        {unit, {:ok, _}}, value -> {unit, {:ok, value}}
        none, _ -> none
      end)
    end)
  rescue
    error ->
      Logger.error(
        "bubble page data #{inspect(source.element)} failed: #{Exception.format_banner(:error, error)}"
      )

      Enum.map(values, fn {unit, _} -> {unit, {:ok, nil}} end)
  end

  # The things `records/5` left as unique IDs in a batch (`{:bubble_ids,
  # ...}`), read once per resource, through Ash with the actor, like
  # `records/5` reads them one by one.
  defp resolve(values, actor) do
    wanted =
      for {_unit, {:ok, {:bubble_ids, resource, value, list?, page_size}}} <- values,
          id <- ids_of(value, list?, page_size),
          reduce: %{} do
        acc -> Map.update(acc, resource, MapSet.new([id]), &MapSet.put(&1, id))
      end

    found = Map.new(wanted, fn {resource, ids} -> {resource, read_ids(actor, resource, ids)} end)

    Enum.map(values, fn
      {unit, {:ok, {:bubble_ids, resource, value, list?, page_size}}} ->
        {unit, {:ok, from_ids(Map.get(found, resource, %{}), value, list?, page_size)}}

      other ->
        other
    end)
  end

  defp ids_of(value, true, page_size),
    do: value |> Enum.take(cap(page_size)) |> Enum.filter(&is_binary/1)

  defp ids_of(value, false, _page_size),
    do: if(is_binary(value) and Regex.match?(@id, value), do: [value], else: [])

  defp from_ids(found, value, true, page_size) do
    value
    |> Enum.take(cap(page_size))
    |> Enum.map(fn
      id when is_binary(id) -> Map.get(found, id)
      record -> record
    end)
    |> Enum.reject(&is_nil/1)
  end

  defp from_ids(found, id, false, _page_size), do: Map.get(found, id)

  defp read_ids(actor, resource, ids) do
    ids = ids |> Enum.uniq() |> Enum.sort()
    [pk] = Ash.Resource.Info.primary_key(resource)
    filter = [{pk, [in: ids]}]

    once({:ids, resource, ids}, actor, fn ->
      resource
      |> Ash.Query.new()
      |> Ash.Query.filter(^filter)
      |> Ash.Query.limit(length(ids))
      |> Ash.read(actor: actor, authorize?: true)
    end)
    |> case do
      {:ok, records} ->
        Map.new(records, &{Map.get(&1, pk), &1})

      {:error, error} ->
        failed(Ash.Query.new(resource), error)
        %{}
    end
  end

  # Values (a thing, a list of things, anything else) with relationships
  # `loads` loaded, one load per resource for all of them; in order.
  defp load_values(values, loads, actor, opts \\ [])
  defp load_values(values, [], _actor, _opts), do: values

  defp load_values(values, loads, actor, opts) do
    by_resource =
      values
      |> Enum.flat_map(&records_in/1)
      |> Enum.group_by(& &1.__struct__)
      |> Map.new(fn {resource, records} ->
        {resource, load_page(records, loads, actor, opts)}
      end)

    {loaded, _} = Enum.map_reduce(values, by_resource, &take_loaded/2)
    loaded
  end

  defp records_in(list) when is_list(list), do: Enum.flat_map(list, &records_in/1)

  defp records_in(%{__struct__: module} = record),
    do: if(Ash.Resource.Info.resource?(module), do: [record], else: [])

  defp records_in(_value), do: []

  defp take_loaded(list, acc) when is_list(list), do: Enum.map_reduce(list, acc, &take_loaded/2)

  defp take_loaded(%{__struct__: module} = record, acc) do
    case Map.get(acc, module) do
      [loaded | rest] -> {loaded, Map.put(acc, module, rest)}
      _ -> {record, acc}
    end
  end

  defp take_loaded(value, acc), do: {value, acc}

  # The reusable instances in repeating group cells (WTF-494): for every
  # surface, each instance in the cells of its lists, one scope per cell
  # (`<%= @web %>.Bubble.cell_scope/4`), read for every cell together
  # (`load_groups/4`); then the instances in their own lists' cells, at
  # most `max_cell_depth/0` levels down and `max_cells/0` scopes in all.
  # The cells are those of the lists just read, as the current user: a
  # thing the user may not read has no cell, and no scope.
  defp load_cells(socket, page, {data, by_source}, only \\ nil),
    do: cell_rounds(socket, BubbleWorkflows.surfaces(page), {data, by_source}, only, [], 0)

  defp cell_rounds(_socket, [], {data, by_source}, _only, cells, _depth),
    do: {data, by_source, cells}

  defp cell_rounds(socket, outer, {data, by_source}, only, cells, depth) do
    # Each instance's scope in every cell (instances before the ones they
    # nest, so their properties are read first), in the lists' order.
    templates =
      for({scope, module} <- outer,
          {rg, entries} <- BubbleWorkflows.cells(module),
          {{rel, inner}, n} <- Enum.with_index(entries),
          cell <- cell_scopes(data, scope, rg),
          do: {{rg, n, rel, inner}, cell <> "-" <> rel})
      |> Enum.uniq_by(&elem(&1, 1))
      |> Enum.sort_by(fn {{rg, n, rel, _}, _} -> {n, rg, rel} end)

    {kept, dropped} =
      if depth >= max_cell_depth(),
        do: {[], templates},
        else: Enum.split(templates, max(max_cells() - length(cells), 0))

    if dropped != [], do: warn_capped()

    if kept == [] do
      {data, by_source, cells}
    else
      batches =
        kept
        |> Enum.group_by(&elem(&1, 0), &elem(&1, 1))
        |> Enum.sort_by(fn {{rg, n, rel, _}, _} -> {n, rg, rel} end)

      # The batches of a round read each other's values (an instance's
      # property, its nested instance's default) in that order (WTF-520).
      groups =
        for {{rg, _n, rel, inner}, scopes} <- batches,
            do: %{module: inner, scopes: scopes, id: {:cells, rg, rel, inner}}

      acc = load_groups(socket, groups, {data, by_source}, only)
      new = for %{module: inner, scopes: scopes} <- groups, scope <- scopes, do: {scope, inner}

      cell_rounds(socket, new, acc, only, cells ++ new, depth + 1)
    end
  end

  # The scopes of a repeating group's cells, by their things (WTF-494); of
  # a repeating group rendered per cell of another (`{outer, inner}`,
  # WTF-520), every inner cell of every outer cell, in the outer cell's
  # scope.
  defp cell_scopes(data, scope, {outer, rg}) do
    for {outer_item, oi} <- cell_items(data, scope, outer),
        outer_scope = Bubble.cell_scope(scope, outer, outer_item, oi),
        {item, i} <- nested_items(data, scope, rg, oi),
        do: Bubble.cell_scope(outer_scope, rg, item, i)
  end

  defp cell_scopes(data, scope, rg),
    do: for({item, i} <- cell_items(data, scope, rg), do: Bubble.cell_scope(scope, rg, item, i))

  # Logged once per page process, not on every read (a keystroke reads).
  defp warn_capped do
    if Process.get(:bubble_cells_capped) != true do
      Process.put(:bubble_cells_capped, true)

      Logger.warning(
        "bubble page data: reusable instances in repeating group cells past " <>
          "#{max_cell_depth()} levels or #{max_cells()} scopes are not read " <>
          "(they show no data and their events are ignored)"
      )
    end
  end

  @doc """
  The most reusable-instance scopes in repeating group cells a page reads
  (`:max_cells`, default `max_items/0` x 10); the first ones are kept.
  """
  def max_cells do
    case Keyword.get(Application.get_env(:<%= @app %>, __MODULE__, []), :max_cells) do
      n when is_integer(n) and n >= 0 -> n
      _ -> max_items() * 10
    end
  end

  @doc """
  How many levels of reusable instances in cells (an instance's own lists'
  cells, ...) a page reads (`:max_cell_depth`, default 3).
  """
  def max_cell_depth do
    case Keyword.get(Application.get_env(:<%= @app %>, __MODULE__, []), :max_cell_depth) do
      n when is_integer(n) and n >= 0 -> n
      _ -> 3
    end
  end

  # What a source's element shows: what a "Display data" step showed in it
  # (WTF-492), which wins over its own source until a reset, read as the
  # current user (in a batch, its relationships load with the others').
  defp shown(shown, source, ctx) do
    page_size =
      case Map.get(source, :display) do
        %{page_size: n} -> n
        _ -> nil
      end

    shown = show(ctx, shown, page_size)

    if ctx.batch,
      do: shown,
      else: load_page(shown, source.loads, ctx.actor)
  rescue
    error ->
      Logger.error(
        "bubble page data #{inspect(source.element)} failed: #{Exception.format_banner(:error, error)}"
      )

      nil
  end

  @doc """
  What a "Display data" step showed (`{resource, list?, value}`, WTF-492),
  as the current user reads it now: a thing's unique ID (a list of them,
  at most `page_size` capped by `max_items/0`) is read again through Ash
  with the actor, so a record the user may not read shows nothing<%= if @enforced? do %> and a
  field the user may not view is empty<% end %>; an ID that is not a text
  shaped like a Bubble ID shows nothing. Any other value is itself.
  Nothing is read with data access off.
  """
  def show(_ctx, {nil, list?, value}, page_size), do: records(nil, nil, value, list?, page_size)

  def show(ctx, {resource, list?, value}, page_size) do
    if data_access?() do
      records(ctx, resource, displayed_ids(value, list?), list?, page_size)
    end
  end

  defp displayed_ids(value, true), do: value |> List.wrap() |> Enum.filter(&bubble_id?/1)
  defp displayed_ids(value, false), do: if(bubble_id?(value), do: value)

  @doc "Whether `value` is a text shaped like a Bubble unique ID."
  def bubble_id?(value), do: is_binary(value) and byte_size(value) <= 64 and Regex.match?(@id, value)

  # One source: its function, then the relationships the page's bindings
  # read through it. A source that fails reads nothing (logged).
  defp run(_module, %{fun: nil}, _ctx), do: nil

  defp run(module, source, %{batch: %{}} = ctx) do
    apply(module, source.fun, [ctx])
  rescue
    error ->
      Logger.error(
        "bubble page data #{inspect(source.element)} failed: #{Exception.format_banner(:error, error)}"
      )

      nil
  end

  defp run(module, source, ctx) do
    module
    |> apply(source.fun, [ctx])
    |> load_page(source.loads, ctx.actor)
  rescue
    error ->
      Logger.error(
        "bubble page data #{inspect(source.element)} failed: #{Exception.format_banner(:error, error)}"
      )

      nil
  end

  # --- reads -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

  @doc """
  Loads a page expression's relationships with a database-side limit on
  the related lists (`related_cap/0`, as for the sources' own loads).
  """
  def load_value(value, loads, ctx) do
    batch = Map.get(ctx, :batch)
    actor? = not is_nil(value) and value === ctx.actor

    cond do
      not data_access?() -> value
      actor? and actor_read?(batch, loads) -> batch.actor
      not actor? and read?(batch, value, loads) -> value
      actor? -> actor_loads(value, loads)
      true -> load_page(value, loads, ctx.actor)
    end
  end

  # The current user with `loads`, read as the current user: once per read
  # of the page's data (`read_pass/1`, WTF-501) for the same paths, however
  # many sources read them. Kept with the actor it was read as (the very
  # term), never served for another.
  defp actor_loads(actor, loads) do
    once({:actor, Enum.sort(loads)}, actor, fn ->
      Runtime.load_page(actor, loads, Runtime.root(nil, actor), related_cap())
    end)
  end

  # `value`'s relationships `loads` (paths of names), read as `actor` with
  # the related lists capped (`related_cap/0`): once per read of the
  # page's data for the very same value and loads (`once/3`, WTF-501), so
  # sources (or the instances of one reusable element in a list's cells)
  # showing the same records load their relationships once.
  defp load_page(value, loads, actor, opts \\ [])
  defp load_page(value, [], _actor, _opts), do: value
  defp load_page(value, _loads, _actor, _opts) when value in [nil, []], do: value

  defp load_page(value, loads, actor, opts) do
    once({:load, value, loads, opts}, actor, fn ->
      Runtime.load_page(value, loads, Runtime.root(nil, actor), related_cap(), opts)
    end)
  end

  @doc """
  `fun`'s result, read once per `read_pass/1` for `key` as `actor` (the
  very term: a result is never served to another actor); outside one,
  `fun` runs every time.
  """
  def once(key, actor, fun) do
    case Process.get(@pass) do
      %{} = pass ->
        case Map.fetch(pass, key) do
          {:ok, {^actor, value}} ->
            value

          _ ->
            value = fun.()
            Process.put(@pass, Map.put(Process.get(@pass), key, {actor, value}))
            value
        end

      _ ->
        fun.()
    end
  end

  # Read for every cell together (WTF-494): what the batch read first, as
  # the current user, for every cell, is not read again: these very
  # records, read with these paths. The current user's relationships come
  # from the batch's copy, never from the actor the policies read (loaded
  # without authorization).
  defp actor_read?(%{actor: copy, actor_paths: paths}, loads) when not is_nil(copy),
    do: Enum.all?(loads, &MapSet.member?(paths, &1))

  defp actor_read?(_batch, _loads), do: false

  defp read?(%{loaded: loaded}, value, loads) do
    records = records_in(value)

    records != [] and
      Enum.all?(records, fn record ->
        case Map.get(loaded, record_key(record)) do
          {^record, paths} -> Enum.all?(loads, &MapSet.member?(paths, &1))
          _ -> false
        end
      end)
  end

  defp read?(_batch, _value, _loads), do: false


  @doc """
  The most related records a loaded relationship reads per record:
  `:max_items`, at most 100. Nested lists share it (a list of lists reads
  at most this many in all, not this many per level).
  """
  def related_cap, do: min(max_items(), 100)

  @doc "A page's thing: the record whose unique ID is in the URL, read through Ash."
  def url_thing(ctx, resource) do
    case ctx.thing do
      id when is_binary(id) -> get(resource, id, ctx)
      _ -> nil
    end
  end

  @doc """
  A query's result: `take` is `:all` (at most the page size, capped at
  `max_items/0`), `:first`, `{:item, n}`, `{:limit, n}` or `:count`.
  The records of a list that holds none (`listed/2` with no IDs) are
  nothing, without a read (WTF-501).
  """
  def read(%Ash.Query{context: %{bubble_listed: 0}}, _ctx, take, _page_size), do: none(take)

<%= if @enforced? do %>  def read(query, ctx, :count, _page_size) do
    # Counted by reading the records' keys through `:search`, not with
    # `Ash.count/2`: Ash's count aggregate under-counts with policies that
    # read the actor (a record the user finds is not counted). At most
    # `max_count/0` are read; past it the count is that cap, logged.
    [pk] = Ash.Resource.Info.primary_key(query.resource)
    cap = max_count()

    query = query |> Ash.Query.select([pk]) |> Ash.Query.limit(cap + 1)

    once({:read, query}, ctx.actor, fn ->
      Ash.read(query, action: read_action(query), actor: ctx.actor, authorize?: true)
    end)
    |> case do
      {:ok, records} when length(records) > cap ->
        Logger.warning(
          "bubble page data: a count of #{inspect(query.resource)} reached :max_count " <>
            "(#{cap}); it shows #{cap}, the true count is larger"
        )

        cap

      {:ok, records} ->
        length(records)

      {:error, error} ->
        failed(query, error)
    end
  end
<% else %>  def read(query, ctx, :count, _page_size) do
    case Ash.count(query, actor: ctx.actor, authorize?: true) do
      {:ok, n} -> n
      {:error, error} -> failed(query, error)
    end
  end
<% end %>
  def read(query, ctx, take, page_size) do
    {offset, limit} =
      case take do
        :all -> {0, listed_cap(query, page_size)}
        :first -> {0, 1}
        {:item, n} -> {n - 1, 1}
        {:limit, n} -> {0, min(cap(page_size), n)}
      end

    query = query |> Ash.Query.offset(offset) |> Ash.Query.limit(limit)

    once({:read, query}, ctx.actor, fn ->
      Ash.read(query, <%= if @enforced? do %>action: read_action(query), <% end %>actor: ctx.actor, authorize?: true)
    end)
    |> case do
      {:ok, records} when take in [:first] or is_tuple(take) and elem(take, 0) == :item ->
        List.first(records)

      {:ok, records} ->
        records

      {:error, error} ->
        failed(query, error)
    end
  end

  defp none(:count), do: 0
  defp none(take) when take in [:all] or (is_tuple(take) and elem(take, 0) == :limit), do: []
  defp none(_take), do: nil

  @doc """
  Marks a query reading the records a list holds (WTF-495: a list of
  things sorted or filtered in the database; `ids` from `listed_ids/1`),
  which `read/4` reads as the user may view them, like reading the
  list's things by ID, rather than as a search (what the user may find);
  all of them when no page shows them, and in the list's order among
  equal sort keys.
  """
  def listed(query, ids) when is_list(ids) do
    [pk | _] = Ash.Resource.Info.primary_key(Ash.Query.new(query).resource)
    key = Ash.Expr.ref(pk)

    # Equal sort keys keep the list's order: its position last.
    position =
      Ash.Expr.calc(fragment(
          "array_position(?::text[], CAST(? AS text))",
          type(^ids, {:array, :string}),
          ^key
        ),
        type: :integer
      )

    query
    |> Ash.Query.new()
    |> Ash.Query.set_context(%{bubble_listed: length(ids)})
    |> Ash.Query.sort([{position, :asc}])
  end

  def listed(query, _ids), do: listed(query, [])

  @doc """
  `listed/2` for the records every cell's list holds at once (WTF-520):
  marked the same, but not sorted by the position in their union (each
  cell's own list orders its records, `cell_read/4`).
  """
  def listed_batch(query, ids) when is_list(ids) do
    query
    |> Ash.Query.new()
    |> Ash.Query.set_context(%{bubble_listed: length(ids)})
  end

  def listed_batch(query, _ids), do: listed_batch(query, [])

  @doc """
  The unique IDs of the things a list holds, in its order, each once, for
  `listed/2`: at most `:max_listed` (default 10_000), logged past it.
  """
  def listed_ids(value) do
    cap = max_listed()
    ids = value |> List.wrap() |> Runtime.ids() |> Kernel.||([]) |> Enum.uniq()

    if length(ids) > cap do
      Logger.warning(
        "bubble page data: a list of #{length(ids)} things reached :max_listed (#{cap}); " <>
          "only its first #{cap} are read"
      )
    end

    Enum.take(ids, cap)
  end

  @doc "The most things a list sorted or filtered in the database reads (`:max_listed`, 10_000)."
  def max_listed do
    case Keyword.get(Application.get_env(:<%= @app %>, __MODULE__, []), :max_listed, 10_000) do
      n when is_integer(n) and n > 0 -> n
      _ -> 10_000
    end
  end

  # A list's records read whole (none past its own length) unless a page
  # shows them (its page size, capped by `max_items/0`).
  defp listed_cap(%Ash.Query{context: %{bubble_listed: n}}, nil) when is_integer(n), do: max(n, 1)
  defp listed_cap(_query, page_size), do: cap(page_size)

<%= if @enforced? do %>  defp read_action(%Ash.Query{context: %{bubble_listed: n}}) when is_integer(n), do: :read
  defp read_action(_query), do: :search

<% end %>  @doc "The most items a list of page size `page_size` reads (capped by `max_items/0`)."
  def cap(nil), do: max_items()
  def cap(n) when is_integer(n) and n > 0, do: min(n, max_items())
  def cap(_), do: max_items()

<%= if @enforced? do %>  # A read the policies refuse outright (e.g. logged out, where every rule
  # reads the user) shows nothing, as in Bubble: not an error.
  defp failed(_query, %Ash.Error.Forbidden{}), do: nil
<% end %>  defp failed(query, error) do
    Logger.error(
      "bubble page data: a read of #{inspect(query.resource)} failed: " <>
        Exception.format_banner(:error, Ash.Error.to_error_class(error))
    )

    nil
  end

  @doc """
  A thing (or list of things) as records of `resource`: records pass,
  Bubble IDs are read through Ash (a list at most its page size, capped by
  `max_items/0`, in its order); anything else is the value itself.
  """
  def records(ctx, resource, value, list?, page_size \\ nil)

  # Read for every cell together (WTF-494): unique IDs are read with the
  # other cells' (`{:bubble_ids, ...}`, resolved by the loader).
  def records(%{batch: %{}}, resource, value, list?, page_size)
      when resource != nil and (is_binary(value) or (list? and is_list(value))),
      do: {:bubble_ids, resource, value, list? and is_list(value), page_size}

  def records(_ctx, nil, value, true, page_size) when is_list(value),
    do: Enum.take(value, cap(page_size))
  def records(_ctx, nil, value, _list?, _page_size), do: value
  def records(_ctx, _resource, nil, _list?, _page_size), do: nil

  def records(ctx, resource, value, true, page_size) when is_list(value) do
    value = Enum.take(value, cap(page_size))
    ids = for id <- value, is_binary(id), do: id

    found = if ids == [], do: %{}, else: read_ids(ctx.actor, resource, ids)

    value
    |> Enum.map(fn
      id when is_binary(id) -> Map.get(found, id)
      record -> record
    end)
    |> Enum.reject(&is_nil/1)
  end

  def records(ctx, resource, id, _list?, _page_size) when is_binary(id), do: get(resource, id, ctx)
  def records(_ctx, _resource, value, _list?, _page_size), do: value

  defp get(resource, id, ctx) do
    if Regex.match?(@id, id) do
      once({:get, resource, id}, ctx.actor, fn ->
        Ash.get(resource, id, actor: ctx.actor, authorize?: true, not_found_error?: false)
      end)
      |> case do
        {:ok, record} -> record
        {:error, error} -> failed(Ash.Query.new(resource), error)
      end
    end
  end

  @doc """
  What a filter reads from the current user: the value at `path` (names),
  after loading the relationships `loads`; nil when logged out.
  """
  def actor(ctx, path, loads) do
    ctx
    |> BubbleWorkflows.actor([])
    |> load_value(loads, ctx)
    |> get_path(path)
  end

  defp get_path(value, []), do: value
  defp get_path(nil, _path), do: nil

  defp get_path(value, [name | rest]) when is_map(value),
    do: value |> Map.get(String.to_existing_atom(name)) |> get_path(rest)

  defp get_path(_value, _path), do: nil

  @doc "A pinned filter value: a thing as its ID, things as their IDs."
  def pin(value, :one), do: Runtime.id(value)
  def pin(value, :many), do: Runtime.ids(value)
  def pin(value, _), do: value

  # --- searches in cells (WTF-520) ----------------------------------------------------

  @doc """
  A search a source reads in a repeating group's cell, read for every
  cell together (see "Searches in cells"). `spec`: the search (`ref`),
  its pins (`pins`, the cell's values), the keys that differ from cell to
  cell (`keys`: `{pin, attribute, :eq | :in, unless}`, a key holding only
  where the pin `unless` is not yes), the yes/no pins making it match
  nothing (`void`: `{pin, :yes}` when yes, `{pin, :no}` unless yes), its sort's attributes (`sort`), how
  much of it is taken (`take`, `page_size`, as `read/4`'s) and the
  relationships read through its records (`loads`). `query` is the cell's
  own query; `batch`, given every cell's values of the keys, the query of
  all of them. The loader collects the cells' searches and reads them
  first (`collect_cells/2`); a cell then finds its records. Outside that
  (a cell nothing collected, a read outside a read of the page's data),
  the cell's own query is read, as any other.
  """
  def cell_read(ctx, spec, query, batch) do
    key = {:cell_read, spec.ref, spec.pins, spec.take, spec.page_size, spec.loads}

    case Process.get(@collect) do
      requests when is_list(requests) ->
        # Collecting: a search read in an earlier round is known (a search
        # reading its records collects its own with them).
        case Process.get(@pass) do
          %{^key => {actor, value}} when actor === ctx.actor ->
            value

          _ ->
            # After a search not read yet, this one's values may be read
            # from its placeholder: collected, but read in a later round.
            request =
              Map.merge(spec, %{
                key: key,
                query: query,
                batch: batch,
                later?: Process.get(@unread, false)
              })

            Process.put(@collect, [request | requests])
            Process.put(@unread, true)
            none(spec.take)
        end

      _ ->
        once(key, ctx.actor, fn ->
          query.()
          |> read(ctx, spec.take, spec.page_size)
          |> load_value(spec.loads, ctx)
        end)
    end
  end

  @doc """
  The most records the query of a round of cells reads, and the most
  combinations of the cells' key values it compares (`:max_batched`,
  default 10_000): past it, each cell's search is read on its own
  (logged).
  """
  def max_batched do
    case Keyword.get(Application.get_env(:<%= @app %>, __MODULE__, []), :max_batched, 10_000) do
      n when is_integer(n) and n > 0 -> n
      _ -> 10_000
    end
  end

  @doc """
  How many rounds of cells' searches a read collects and reads together
  (`:max_cell_rounds`, default 4): a search reading another's records is
  collected in the round after it, and a page's sizes left short are read
  again in a round of their own. Past it, what is left is read cell by
  cell (logged).
  """
  def max_cell_rounds do
    case Keyword.get(Application.get_env(:<%= @app %>, __MODULE__, []), :max_cell_rounds, 4) do
      n when is_integer(n) and n > 0 -> n
      _ -> 4
    end
  end

  # Runs `fun` (a source in every unit) collecting the searches it reads
  # in cells (`cell_read/4`, which reads nothing then), and reads them
  # for every cell together into the read pass, where each cell finds
  # its part. A search whose constraints read another one's records is
  # collected once those are read: rounds until nothing new is collected,
  # at most `max_cell_rounds/0`; past it the cells left read their own
  # queries (logged). Every search collected is settled in the pass, read
  # together or alone, so a later round never collects it again. Nothing
  # is kept outside a read pass.
  defp collect_cells(fun, actor, round \\ 1) do
    if is_map(Process.get(@pass)) do
      collected = collect(fun, actor)
      # A search collected after one not read yet waits for a later round.
      new = collected |> Enum.reject(& &1.later?) |> Enum.uniq_by(& &1.key)

      cond do
        collected == [] ->
          :ok

        round > max_cell_rounds() ->
          cells_warning(
            "searches in repeating group cells past #{max_cell_rounds()} rounds " <>
              "(:max_cell_rounds) are read cell by cell"
          )

        true ->
          new
          |> Enum.group_by(&{&1.ref, &1.take, &1.page_size, &1.loads, shared_pins(&1)})
          |> Enum.each(fn {_shape, group} -> read_cells(group, actor) end)

          collect_cells(fun, actor, round + 1)
      end
    end
  end

  # The searches `fun` reads in cells that the pass does not hold yet.
  defp collect(fun, actor) do
    previous = Process.put(@collect, [])

    requests =
      try do
        fun.()
        Process.get(@collect)
      after
        if previous, do: Process.put(@collect, previous), else: Process.delete(@collect)
        Process.delete(@unread)
      end

    requests
    |> Enum.reverse()
    |> Enum.reject(&read_already?(&1.key, actor))
  end

  defp read_already?(key, actor), do: match?(%{^key => {^actor, _}}, Process.get(@pass))

  # Logged once per page process, not on every read.
  defp cells_warning(message) do
    if Process.get({:bubble_cells_warned, message}) != true do
      Process.put({:bubble_cells_warned, message}, true)
      Logger.warning("bubble page data: " <> message)
    end
  end

  # The pins every cell of a group has alike: all but its keys.
  defp shared_pins(request),
    do: Map.drop(request.pins, for({var, _attr, _kind, _unless} <- request.keys, do: var))

  # The cells of one search whose pins differ only in their keys: their
  # keys hold or not alike (`unless` is a shared pin). A cell with a key
  # whose value is empty reads its own query (cells alike share it); one
  # whose list is empty finds nothing (the key is a part of the search's
  # conjunction). What is read is kept in the pass: settled.
  defp read_cells([first | _] = group, actor) do
    active =
      for {var, attr, kind, unless} <- first.keys,
          is_nil(unless) or Map.get(first.pins, unless) != true,
          do: {var, attr, kind}

    # A cell whose empty value the search does not ignore finds nothing.
    {void, group} =
      Enum.split_with(group, fn r -> Enum.any?(Map.get(r, :void, []), &void?(&1, r.pins)) end)

    {keyed, alone} =
      Enum.split_with(group, fn r ->
        active != [] and Enum.all?(active, fn {var, _, kind} -> keyed?(r.pins[var], kind) end)
      end)

    {none, keyed} =
      Enum.split_with(keyed, fn r ->
        Enum.any?(active, fn {var, _, _} -> key_values(r.pins[var]) == [] end)
      end)

    # Every cell's combinations of its keys' values: past `max_batched/0`,
    # the cells read their own queries (logged once).
    combinations = keyed |> Enum.map(&length(tuples(&1, active))) |> Enum.sum()

    found =
      cond do
        keyed == [] ->
          %{}

        combinations > max_batched() ->
          cells_warning(
            "a search in repeating group cells has #{combinations} key combinations, " <>
              "past :max_batched (#{max_batched()}); its cells are read cell by cell"
          )

          read_alone(keyed, actor)

        true ->
          batch_results(keyed, active, first, actor)
      end

    found = Enum.reduce(none ++ void, found, &Map.put(&2, &1.key, none(&1.take)))
    found = Map.merge(found, read_alone(alone, actor))

    keys = Map.keys(found)
    values = found |> Map.values() |> load_values(first.loads, actor)

    Process.put(
      @pass,
      Enum.reduce(Enum.zip(keys, values), Process.get(@pass), fn {key, value}, pass ->
        Map.put(pass, key, {actor, value})
      end)
    )
  end

  defp void?({var, :yes}, pins), do: Map.get(pins, var) == true
  defp void?({var, :no}, pins), do: Map.get(pins, var) != true

  # Each cell's own query, as `cell_read/4` reads it alone (identical ones
  # once).
  defp read_alone(requests, actor) do
    ctx = %{actor: actor}

    Map.new(requests, fn r ->
      {r.key,
       once({:cell_alone, r.key}, actor, fn -> r.query.() |> read(ctx, r.take, r.page_size) end)}
    end)
  end

  defp keyed?(value, :eq), do: is_binary(value)
  defp keyed?(value, :in), do: is_list(value)

  defp key_values(value) when is_binary(value), do: [value]
  defp key_values(values) when is_list(values), do: values |> Enum.filter(&is_binary/1) |> Enum.uniq()
  defp key_values(_value), do: []

  # A cell's key tuples: each combination of its keys' values.
  defp tuples(request, active) do
    Enum.reduce(active, [[]], fn {var, _attr, _kind}, acc ->
      for t <- acc, v <- key_values(request.pins[var]), do: [v | t]
    end)
    |> Enum.map(&(&1 |> Enum.reverse() |> List.to_tuple()))
  end

  defp row_tuple(row, active),
    do: active |> Enum.map(fn {_var, attr, _kind} -> Map.get(row, attr) end) |> List.to_tuple()

  # The query of `requests` together: each active key compared with all
  # their values, and with two or three keys the cells' own combinations
  # of them (no record of one cell's first key and another's second).
  defp batch_query(requests, active, first) do
    unions =
      Map.new(active, fn {var, _attr, _kind} ->
        {var, requests |> Enum.flat_map(&key_values(&1.pins[var])) |> Enum.uniq()}
      end)

    query = first.batch.(Map.merge(first.pins, unions))

    case active do
      [_] ->
        query

      _ ->
        columns =
          requests
          |> Enum.flat_map(&tuples(&1, active))
          |> Enum.uniq()
          |> Enum.map(&Tuple.to_list/1)
          |> Enum.zip_with(& &1)

        combined(query, Enum.map(active, fn {_var, attr, _kind} -> Ash.Expr.ref(attr) end), columns)
    end
  end

  defp combined(query, [a, b], [x, y]) do
    Ash.Query.filter(
      query,
      fragment(
        "(CAST(? AS text), CAST(? AS text)) IN (SELECT * FROM unnest(?::text[], ?::text[]))",
        ^a,
        ^b,
        type(^x, {:array, :string}),
        type(^y, {:array, :string})
      )
    )
  end

  defp combined(query, [a, b, c], [x, y, z]) do
    Ash.Query.filter(
      query,
      fragment(
        "(CAST(? AS text), CAST(? AS text), CAST(? AS text)) IN (SELECT * FROM unnest(?::text[], ?::text[], ?::text[]))",
        ^a,
        ^b,
        ^c,
        type(^x, {:array, :string}),
        type(^y, {:array, :string}),
        type(^z, {:array, :string})
      )
    )
  end

  # The rows of each cell, in the read's order: rows grouped once by their
  # keys' values, each cell's tuples looked up.
  defp by_cell(rows, requests, active) do
    index =
      rows
      |> Enum.with_index()
      |> Enum.group_by(fn {row, _i} -> row_tuple(row, active) end)

    Map.new(requests, fn r ->
      mine =
        r
        |> tuples(active)
        |> Enum.flat_map(&Map.get(index, &1, []))
        |> Enum.uniq_by(&elem(&1, 1))
        |> Enum.sort_by(&elem(&1, 1))
        |> Enum.map(&elem(&1, 0))

      {r.key, mine}
    end)
  end

  # `%{key => value}` for each request, as its own query would read it. A
  # read that fails leaves every cell of it empty (logged), as each cell's
  # own read would.
  defp batch_results(requests, active, first, actor) do
    query = batch_query(requests, active, first)

    case query do
      %Ash.Query{context: %{bubble_listed: n}} when is_integer(n) ->
        listed_results(query, requests, active, first, actor)

      _ when first.take == :count ->
        count_results(query, requests, active, actor)

      _ when first.take in [:first, {:item, 1}] ->
        if Enum.all?(active, &match?({_var, _attr, :eq}, &1)),
          do: first_results(query, requests, active, actor),
          else: round_results(requests, active, first, actor, %{}, 1)

      _ ->
        round_results(requests, active, first, actor, %{}, 1)
    end
  end

  # A count: the records' keys, counted per cell. Past `max_batched/0` the
  # cells' counts are read on their own (logged once).
  defp count_results(query, requests, active, actor) do
    [pk | _] = Ash.Resource.Info.primary_key(query.resource)
    attrs = Enum.uniq([pk | for({_var, attr, _kind} <- active, do: attr)])
    cap = max_batched()
    query = query |> Ash.Query.select(attrs) |> Ash.Query.limit(cap + 1)

    case batch_read(query, actor) do
      {:ok, rows} when length(rows) > cap ->
        cells_warning(
          "a count of #{inspect(query.resource)} in repeating group cells reached " <>
            ":max_batched (#{cap}); each cell's count is read on its own"
        )

        read_alone(requests, actor)

      {:ok, rows} ->
        rows
        |> by_cell(requests, active)
        |> Map.new(fn {key, mine} -> {key, cell_count(length(mine), query)} end)

      {:error, error} ->
        failed(query, error)
        Map.new(requests, &{&1.key, nil})
    end
  end

<%= if @enforced? do %>  defp cell_count(n, query) do
    cap = max_count()

    if n > cap do
      Logger.warning(
        "bubble page data: a count of #{inspect(query.resource)} reached :max_count " <>
          "(#{cap}); it shows #{cap}, the true count is larger"
      )

      cap
    else
      n
    end
  end
<% else %>  defp cell_count(n, _query), do: n
<% end %>
  # A first item: the first record of each cell's keys, in the search's
  # order (`DISTINCT ON` the keys), one per cell at most.
  defp first_results(query, requests, active, actor) do
    query = Ash.Query.distinct(query, for({_var, attr, _kind} <- active, do: attr))

    case batch_read(query, actor) do
      {:ok, rows} ->
        rows |> by_cell(requests, active) |> Map.new(fn {key, mine} -> {key, List.first(mine)} end)

      {:error, error} ->
        failed(query, error)
        Map.new(requests, &{&1.key, nil})
    end
  end

  # The records a list holds (WTF-495): all of every cell's at once (the
  # query reads no more than their IDs, in the search's order only:
  # `listed_batch/2`), each cell's in its own list's order among equal
  # sort keys.
  defp listed_results(query, requests, active, first, actor) do
    query = Ash.Query.limit(query, max(query.context.bubble_listed, 1))
    [pk | _] = Ash.Resource.Info.primary_key(query.resource)
    by_key = Map.new(requests, &{&1.key, &1})

    case batch_read(query, actor) do
      {:ok, rows} ->
        rows
        |> by_cell(requests, active)
        |> Map.new(fn {key, mine} ->
          r = by_key[key]
          mine = list_order(mine, r, pk, active, first.sort)

          if r.take == :count,
            do: {key, cell_count(length(mine), query)},
            else: {key, taken(mine, r, true)}
        end)

      {:error, error} ->
        failed(query, error)
        Map.new(requests, &{&1.key, nil})
    end
  end

  # Among records with equal sort keys (contiguous in the read), a cell's
  # own list's order (its `:in` key on the primary key).
  defp list_order(rows, request, pk, active, sort) do
    position =
      case Enum.find(active, fn {_var, attr, kind} -> kind == :in and attr == pk end) do
        {var, _, _} -> request.pins[var] |> key_values() |> Enum.with_index() |> Map.new()
        nil -> %{}
      end

    rows
    |> Enum.chunk_by(fn row -> Enum.map(sort, &Map.get(row, &1)) end)
    |> Enum.flat_map(fn run -> Enum.sort_by(run, &Map.get(position, Map.get(&1, pk))) end)
  end

  # Records sorted by the search and cut per cell. Every record read is
  # some cell's (the keys, and their combinations, are the cells' own), so
  # a read past the sum of the cells' needs settles at least one cell: a
  # cell with fewer than its need in a read that reached its limit may
  # have lost records to others, and is read again with the other such
  # cells, the limit doubled each round. Past `max_cell_rounds/0` rounds,
  # or a round that settles no cell, the cells left read their own
  # queries (logged).
  defp round_results([], _active, _first, _actor, acc, _round), do: acc

  defp round_results(requests, active, first, actor, acc, round) do
    # Doubled each round, never past `max_batched/0` (plus one): past it a
    # round may settle no cell, and they read their own queries.
    limit =
      min(
        (requests |> Enum.map(&needed(&1, false)) |> Enum.sum()) * 2 ** (round - 1) + 1,
        max_batched() + 1
      )

    query = requests |> batch_query(active, first) |> Ash.Query.limit(limit)
    by_key = Map.new(requests, &{&1.key, &1})

    case batch_read(query, actor) do
      {:ok, rows} ->
        full? = length(rows) >= limit

        {acc, left} =
          rows
          |> by_cell(requests, active)
          |> Enum.reduce({acc, []}, fn {key, mine}, {acc, left} ->
            r = by_key[key]
            mine = Enum.take(mine, needed(r, false))

            if full? and length(mine) < needed(r, false),
              do: {acc, [r | left]},
              else: {Map.put(acc, key, taken(mine, r, false)), left}
          end)

        cond do
          left == [] ->
            acc

          length(left) == length(requests) or round >= max_cell_rounds() ->
            cells_warning(
              "a search of #{inspect(query.resource)} in repeating group cells left cells " <>
                "short after #{round} rounds; they are read cell by cell"
            )

            Map.merge(acc, read_alone(left, actor))

          true ->
            round_results(left, active, first, actor, acc, round + 1)
        end

      {:error, error} ->
        failed(query, error)
        Map.merge(acc, Map.new(requests, &{&1.key, nil}))
    end
  end

  # How many of a cell's records its own read takes (`read/4`).
  defp needed(r, listed?) do
    case r.take do
      :first -> 1
      {:item, n} -> n
      {:limit, n} -> min(cap(r.page_size), n)
      :all when listed? and is_nil(r.page_size) -> max(r.query.().context.bubble_listed, 1)
      :all -> cap(r.page_size)
    end
  end

  defp taken(mine, r, listed?) do
    mine = Enum.take(mine, needed(r, listed?))

    case r.take do
      :first -> List.first(mine)
      {:item, n} -> Enum.at(mine, n - 1)
      _ -> mine
    end
  end

  defp batch_read(query, actor),
    do:
      Ash.read(query, <%= if @enforced? do %>action: read_action(query), <% end %>actor: actor, authorize?: true)

  # --- reactivity ------------------------------------------------------------------------

  # A value over queries (WTF-495) follows their resources' changes too.
  defp topics(topics, %{query_topics: resources} = source, value) when is_list(resources) do
    resources
    |> Enum.reduce(topics, &MapSet.put(&2, Changes.topic(&1)))
    |> topics(Map.delete(source, :query_topics), value)
  end

  defp topics(topics, %{topic: nil}, _value), do: topics

  defp topics(topics, %{topic: type} = source, value) do
    topics = if source.read == :query, do: MapSet.put(topics, Changes.topic(type)), else: topics
    record_topics(topics, value, source.loads)
  end

  defp record_topics(topics, values, loads) when is_list(values),
    do: Enum.reduce(values, topics, &record_topics(&2, &1, loads))

  defp record_topics(topics, %{__struct__: resource} = record, loads) do
    type = resource |> Module.split() |> List.last()

    topics =
      case Ash.Resource.Info.primary_key(resource) do
        [pk] -> MapSet.put(topics, Changes.topic(type, Map.get(record, pk)))
        _ -> topics
      end

    Enum.reduce(loads, topics, fn [name | rest], acc ->
      related = Map.get(record, String.to_existing_atom(name))
      record_topics(acc, related, if(rest == [], do: [], else: [rest]))
    end)
  rescue
    _ -> topics
  end

  defp record_topics(topics, _value, _loads), do: topics

  defp subscribe(socket, topics) do
    if connected?(socket) do
      old = Map.get(socket.assigns, :bubble_topics, MapSet.new())

      for topic <- MapSet.difference(topics, old), do: Changes.subscribe(topic)
      for topic <- MapSet.difference(old, topics), do: Changes.unsubscribe(topic)

      assign(socket, :bubble_topics, topics)
    else
      socket
    end
  end
end
